      "username": "PlatinumWarlock",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/platinumwarlock/{size}/1869_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-03-29T20:43:02.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"MindWanderer\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mindwanderer/48/4816_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> MindWanderer:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Jeysie wrote:</b><br><blockquote>And yeah I'm also kinda with speedyolrac in the \"I would rather simply play an actual RPG\" bucket, especially since that's a far cheaper route.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nYeah, even at, say, $40 for the core rulebook, $10-$20 per adventure set, and $30-$40 per supplement, it'll take a lot of material to add up to the cost of one Gloomhaven.&nbsp; And with that, you get a lot more flexibility and story.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Beyond that, most PDFs are much cheaper than their hard copy counterparts.&nbsp; Get yourself a cheap tablet and load it full of PDFs, and you've got an easy-to-use rpg library that fits in a backpack or purse.</p>",
