      "created_at": "2018-04-03T14:33:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I do love paging through the books, being able to hook my fingers through multiple pages and flip around quickly is nice. Though my only experience with PDF rule books is Pathfinder and they don't have hyperlinked text to my knowledge, without the links it's actually harder to use the PDF instead of the normal book, but i also understand the weight problem, I had screwed some wheels and a handle to an old milk crate, Not sure if it broke because of the wight or because i put the screws in the wrong place but w/e</p>",
